 ('p','What we found: We recorded five full cycles and analysed cycles 2–5. A cycle runs between successive upward crossings of the water surface. Table 1 compares all 14 accepted cases.'),
 ('small','Fx is the horizontal force along the fixed domain. Fz is the vertical force after we subtract buoyancy. Buoyancy is the upward force from displaced water. ΔFx and ΔFz show changes from the calm case C01.'),
