 ('table',1),
 ('h2','Checking numerical accuracy first'),
 ('small','What we found: Our GPU timing estimate is 17.6 h for W05 at Δt/2 and 35.3 h at Δt/4. GPU hours mean elapsed time on the graphics processor. We used 1.36 s per step from the existing run.'),
 ('small','Why: VOF follows the fraction of each cell filled with water. HRIC keeps the calculated water–air boundary sharp. The Courant number measures how far fluid travels per step relative to one cell. CFLi is its maximum near that boundary. Our upper HRIC limit is 1.00, but recorded CFLi maxima reach 1.90–2.00. The calculation may weaken incoming waves. The W04e saved-step peak is at x = −11.9 m. Measured heights are 0.96–0.99 of their targets in the attenuated cases.'),
